You are an expert systems architect analyzing inference cost scaling.

===========================================================
ARCHITECTURE CONTEXT
AMF (Adaptive Memory Fabric) is a deterministic inference memory system
designed to eliminate redundant prompt computation by replaying previously
computed prefix states. AMF operates below the model layer and above the
kernel layer, enforcing strict determinism, ROI-based admission control,
and monotonic policy updates.

AMF stores:
- KV cache states
- Model execution metadata
- Deterministic sampling context
- Restore cost statistics
- Saved compute estimates

The system guarantees:
- Replay only under deterministic sampling
- ROI must exceed 1.0
- Negative ROI disables replay
- Fail-closed behavior on uncertainty

